T.T version; rel = |r_red|/max(ref,1).\n  - Verify deep immutability: compare states snapshot vs after (deep equality), u unchanged.\n- Print a JSON report to stdout (and the harness captures it).\n\nOne question: does `_assemble_nonlinear_system` need `committed_states` in a specific form (e.g., NonlinearStateStore or dict of per-element states)? res.element_states is Dict[int, Any]. The ep_isolation run() reads res.element_states.values() as dicts. OK.\n\nAlso num_layers default is 5 in solve_static_nonlinear. Use 5.\n\nLet me check _assemble_nonlinear_system_unchecked quickly for the corotational_tangent handling with tangent=False, and whether it mutates committed_states. Actually the docstring says the reference assembler opens a persistent trial transaction before invoking any element; committed state remains reusable. I'll trust plus verify via deep compare.\n\nOne more thing: the model after solve may have been mutated (e.g., element internal caches), but for the independent assembly we reuse the same model — that's what the solver's own postcheck does. Fine.\n\nEdge: `_assemble_nonlinear_system` signature: (model, displacements, committed_states, num_layers, tangent=True, ...). Good.\n\nLet me also confirm `build_constraint_transformation` import path: from anysolver.assembly import build_constraint_transformation (used in convergence_study.py). And assemble_stiffness_matrix from anysolver.matrix_assembly. assemble_load_vector from anysolver.matrix_assembly.\n\nNow about \"Verify deep input-state immutability\": also verify that passing initial state to the solve isn't relevant here (we don't pass initial states). The \"input-state\" refers to the state used for the independent residual reconstruction (copied state) — verify the copies are not mutated by the assembly, and that res.displacements/element_states themselves are not mutated by our reconstruction. I'll check both.\n\nLet me write the script. Also include the VK elastic/plastic -6k cases in the sa