{"id": "reasoning-5bfd1f45-1af9-5151-9690-6ef3fd0cb95a-0", "sessionId": "b9a80757-48a2-a90d-2f72-692761706b93", "turnId": "turn-8c7e0354138e253f073f636b837c66de", "createdAt": 1792345851454, "updatedAt": 1792345851454, "generationStatus": "completed", "relatedEntryId": null, "type": "reasoning", "text": "Now write diagnostics/ep_attribution.py. Preserve original diagnostic files — I'm adding a new file, not replacing. Good.\n\nThe script:\n\n```python\n\"\"\"Bounded plastic attribution batch (Slice 3 deliverable 2)...\"\"\"\nimport copy, json, sys, os\nsys.path.insert(0, os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__)))\nimport numpy as np\nfrom ep_isolation import shell_model\nfrom anysolver import solve_static_nonlinear\nfrom anysolver.assembly import build_constraint_transformation\nfrom anysolver.matrix_assembly import assemble_load_vector, assemble_stiffness_matrix\nfrom anysolver.nonlinear_static import _assemble_nonlinear_system\nfrom anysolver.corotational import build_nonlinear_rotating_mpc_map\n\nCASES = {\n  \"cr_plastic_6k\": (\"corotational\", 1.0, -6000.0),\n  \"cr_plastic_10k\": (\"corotational\", 1.0, -10000.0),\n  \"cr_plastic_14k\": (\"corotational\", 1.0, -14000.0),\n  \"vk_elastic_6k\": (\"von_karman\", 1e4, -6000.0),\n  \"vk_plastic_6k\": (\"von_karman\", 1.0, -6000.0),\n}\n```\n\nFor each: build model via shell_model(scale, True, fz) → (m, lc, probe). Solve: solve_static_nonlinear(m, lc, kinematics=kin, num_steps=6, max_iterations=30, record_increment_snapshots=True). Default tolerance 1e-6 (don't pass).\n\nThen instrumentation + independent residual.\n\nDeep compare of states: states may contain numpy arrays; use a recursive equality check or compare repr? Better: pickle-free deep compare via np.testing on arrays. Simple approach: snapshot = copy.deepcopy(res.element_states); after assembly compare with a helper `states_equal(a, b)` that walks dicts/lists/arrays.\n\nAlso verify u immutability: u_before = res.displacements.copy(); after, np.array_equal.\n\nAlso verify the model's probe uz from res.displacements.\n\nIndependent residual:\n```\nK0, _ = assemble_stiffness_matrix(m)\nF_prop, _ = assemble_load_vector(m, lc)\n_, _, T, u0, _, _ = build_constraint_transformation(K0, F_prop, m)\nmpc = build_nonlinear_rotating_mpc_map(m, T) if kin == \"corotational\" else None\nstates_for_assembly = copy.deepcopy(res.element_states)\nF_int, _, _ = _assemble_nonlinear_system(m, u, states_for_assembly, 5, tangent=False, kinematics=kin, corotational_tangent=(\"work_conjugate\" if kin==\"corotational\" else \"auto\"))\n```\n\nHmm — what does the solver pass for corotational_tangent in assembly? For force control with kinematics corotational, resolved tangent is auto→work_conjugate for coupled models. For F_int only (tangent=False), the tangent mode likely doesn't matter. But to be safe pass \"work_conjugate\" for corotational. Let me check _assemble_nonlinear_system_unchecked briefly to see if corotational_tangent affects force. Search for corotational_tangent in that function.\n\nActually, let me check quickly with grep in the unchecked function region (1270-1605).", "summary": []}
