   cancellation_token=cancellation_token,\n8347:                cancellation_token=cancellation_token,\n    def cancellation_checkpoint(stage: str, *, context: str) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n        \"\"\"Run one cancellation checkpoint, then the matching lifecycle guard.\n\n        An absent token or an exact, unmodified ``CancellationToken`` can only\n        run the solver's own checkpoint code.  The token is verified *before*\n        that code runs and again afterwards: checking only afterwards would let\n        a token repair itself inside the checkpoint and still be trusted.  A\n        replaced checkpoint and any other token remain hostile observation\n        boundaries and keep the complete lifecycle scan.\n        \"\"\"\n\n        known_before = _is_known_cancellation_checkpoint(cancellation_token)\n        cancellation_safe_point(cancellation_token, stage)\n        if known_before and _is_known_cancellation_checkpoint(cancellation_token):\n            return internal_guard(model, context=context)\n        if cancellation_token is not None:\n            record_nonlinear_solver_event(\"qualified_guard_untrusted_token\")\n        return exact_guard(model, context=context)\n\n    exact_guard(model, context=\"nonlinear static solve preflight\")\n    cancellation_safe_point(cancellation_token, \"nonlinear_static.start\")\n    exact_guard(model, context=\"nonlinear static start cancellation\")\n    owned_config = _owned_nonlinear_static_operation_config(\n        model,\n        max_load_factor=max_load_factor,\n        num_steps=num_steps,\n        max_iterations=max_iterations,\n        tolerance=tolerance,\n        num_layers=num_layers,\n        min_step_fraction=min_step_fraction,\n        control=control,\n        kinematics=kinematics,\n        corotational_tangent=corotational_tangent,\n        equilibrate_initial_state=equilibrate_initial_state,\n        record_increment_snapshots=record_increment_snapshots,\n        emit_restart_checkpoint=emit_restart_checkpoint,\n", "durationMs": 0.0, "display": {"success": true, "verb": "Ran", "message": "cd \"C:/Github/ANYsolver\" && grep -n \"SolveCancelled\\|cancellation_token\\|def cancellation_checkpoint\" src/anysolver/nonlinear_static.py | head -25 && sed -n '5125,5160p' src/anysolver/nonlinear_static.py", "warnings": [], "approvalNote": null, "suffix": ""}, "decision": "execute", "approvalType": "always", "approvalSource": "bypass"}}
{"id": "reasoning-c93617ab-5154-5ac0-b99e-ffe45bba46c0-0", "sessionId": "b9a80757-48a2-a90d-2f72-692761706b93", "turnId": "turn-8c7e0354138e253f073f636b837c66de", "createdAt": 1792346364482, "updatedAt": 1792346364482, "generationStatus": "completed", "relatedEntryId": null, "type": "reasoning", "text": "Cancellation raises SolveCancelled at safe points (exception propagates; no result object). So for the cancellation integrity check: catch SolveCancelled, then verify (a) the caller's restart input (the checkpoint dict passed in) is deep-unchanged, (b) the model's committed state... \"accepted snapshots intact\" — since the exception carries no result, the meaningful integrity checks are: the caller's restart checkpoint input is unchanged, and a subsequent resume from that same checkpoint input still works and reproduces the uninterrupted continuation (i.e., the cancelled run left no residue in the caller's inputs). Also for a fresh (non-restart) cancelled run: the model object remains usable and a re-solve from scratch reproduces the uninterrupted result.\n\nAdditionally \"rejected steps\" integrity: during the DC split runs, cutbacks occur (rejected increments); the accepted snapshots (record_increment_snapshots=True) must correspond only to committed steps — verify snapshot count == len(steps) and snapshot load factors/control values match the steps' committed values, and each snapshot's displacements are read-only (flags write=False) and element states are owned copies.\n\nThat's a reasonable interpretation. Now write the script. To keep each harness attempt ≤120s, structure it with subcommands:\n\n- `preyield` — 4 solves (direct/interp × plastic/elastic) at 6 steps: fast (small model, pre-yield converges in ~5 iters). Probably ~10-20s total.\n- `dc_direct` — uninterrupted DC direct + split/resume + comparisons. Uninterrupted 12 steps at 1e-8... could be slow. Maybe 60-90s. Split adds another ~equal amount → might exceed 120s. Separate: `dc_direct_full` (uninterrupted only) and `dc_direct_split` (half + resume + compare, needs uninterrupted result — recompute? That doubles cost. Better: dc_direct does full + split in one attempt if it fits in 120s; risky.\n\nAlternative: cache the uninterrupted result to a JSON/npz in the evidence dir? Results contain element states (dicts with arrays) — serializing is complex. Simpler: run full and split in the same process, one attempt, timeout 120s. If the model is small (2 shell + 2 beam elements, ~15 nodes), 12 DC steps at 1e-8 with 40 max iters — the force runs at 6 steps took 50s mostly due to plastic fiber iterations and cutbacks near collapse. DC through the limit point may need many cutbacks... could exceed 120s. Hmm.\n\nThe assignment fixes the parameters: num_steps12, max_iterations40, tolerance1e-8. Individual diagnostic ≤120s. If the direct DC full+split doesn't fit in 120s, I have a problem: the assignment says individual diagnostic <=120s. But maybe DC on this small model is fast — the corotational elastic convergence runs R1 (4x1 shell + 2 beam) took 2.7s for 4 steps. Plastic DC 12 steps maybe 30-60s. Full+split ≈ 2× uninterrupted ≈ maybe 120s. Tight.\n\nPlan: `dc` subcommand runs: full direct, split direct (half+resume), full interp, split interp, cancellation probe — all in one process streaming per-stage JSON, timeout 120s. If it times out, I see how far it got and split into separate attempts by stage with an attempt cache... Let me structure stages as separate subcommands so I can budget precisely:\n\n- `preyield`\n- `dc_full DIRECT|INTERP` (uninterrupted; also emits restart checkpoint; prints result summary JSON)\n- `dc_split DIRECT|INTERP` (half + resume; needs uninterrupted for comparison — recompute uninterrupted in-process; cost 2×)\n- `dc_cancel DIRECT` (cancellation integrity)\n\ndc_split recomputes uninterrupted → total for direct = full(1) + split(2) + cancel(1) ≈ 4× uninterrupted time. If uninterrupted is ~30s → 120s across 3 attempts. OK.\n\nActually, to compare split vs uninterrupted, the split attempt itself can run uninterrupted + half + resume (3 solves) in one process — that guarantees identical comparison and costs 3× uninterrupted in one 120s attempt. If uninterrupted ≈ 25-35s, 3× ≈ 75-105s. Feasible but tight. Let me first measure with `dc_full direct` alone.\n\nAlso the independent residual ≤1e-7 and constraint postcheck and reactions for the DC runs — include in dc_full report (reuse attribution-style residual code). I'll factor a small shared helper... simplest: duplicate the residual function in this script (diagnostics, fine).\n\nLet me now write ep_edge_coupling.py.", "summary": []}
{"id": "assistant-c93617ab-5154-5ac0-b99e-ffe45bba46c0", "sessionId": "b9a80757-48a2-a90d-2f72-692761706b93", "turnId": "turn-8c7e0354138e253f073f636b837c66de", "createdAt": 1792346364482, "updatedAt": 1792346364482, "generationStatus": "completed", "relatedEntryId": null, "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Cancellation raises `SolveCancelled` (no result object), so integrity means: caller's restart input deep-unchanged, and the same checkpoint still resumes correctly afterwards. Writing the deliverable-3 script with staged subcommands so each harness attempt stays under 120s:"}], "source": "harness", "userDisplayContent": null}
{"id": "effect-3a41dddc-ee9f-59c1-90f7-2a3a8ba6c233", "sessionId": "b9a80757-48a2-a90d-2f72-692761706b93", "turnId": "turn-8c7e0354138e253f073f636b837c66de", "createdAt": 1792346364510, "updatedAt": 1792346364555, "generationStatus": "completed", "relatedEntryId": null, "type": "effect", "title": "file_system.write_file", "detail": {"toolName": "file_system.write_file", "display": {"summary": "Writing C:\\Github\\ANYsolver\\.development\\nonlinear-master-slave-coupling-20261017\\diagnostics\\ep_edge_coupling.py", "content": "\"\"\"Slice 3 deliverable 3: direct vs interpolated edge coupling, EP geometry.\n\nExisting EP isolation geometry and repository S355 curve (ep_isolation.py):\nL=1.0, W=0.24, t=0.012, shell 2x1, stiffener 10x40 mm at e=+0.04,\nfiber plasticity. Direct coupling: beam with 2 elements (nodes on shell\nedge nodes). Interpolated counterpart: beam with 3 elements (middle nodes\ngenuinely interpolated on the edge).\n\nStages (streamed as JSON, one per line, flush immediately):\n  preyield                 -2 kN/node force control, plastic vs elastic,\n                            direct and interpolated: lambda=1, zero plastic\n                            strain, plastic == elastic control.\n  dc_full DIRECT|INTERP    uninterrupted DC uz=-0.20 at the original tip\n                            probe (num_steps=12, max_iterations=40,\n                            tolerance=1e-8): completion, target error,\n                            positive plastic strain, independent reduced\n                            residual, constraint postcheck, reactions.\n  dc_split DIRECT|INTERP  split at uz=-0.10, resume to -0.20, compare\n                            u/lambda/history with the uninterrupted run\n                            (same tolerances, no relaxation).\n  dc_cancel DIRECT         cancellation during a resumed run: caller restart\n                            input deep-unchanged, accepted snapshots only\n                            from committed steps, checkpoint still resumes.\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport copy\nimport json\nimport os\nimport sys\n\nsys.path.insert(0, os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__)))\n\nimport numpy as np\n\nfrom ep_isolation import CS, L, NX, NY, R, W, material, t  # noqa: E402\nfrom anysolver import (  # noqa: E402\n    BoundaryCondition,\n    FEModel,\n    LoadCase,\n    create_shell_element,\n    solve_static_nonlinear,\n)\nfrom anysolver.assembly import build_constraint_transformation  # noqa: E402\nfrom anysolver.control import CancellationToken  # noqa: E402\nfrom anysolver.corotational import build_nonlinear_rotating_mpc_map  # noqa: E402\nfrom anysolver.elements import BeamElement, CoupledBeamShellElement  # noqa: E402\nfrom anysolver.matrix_assembly import (  # noqa: E402\n    assemble_load_vector,\n    assemble_stiffness_matrix,\n)\nfrom anysolver.mesh_gen import InterpolatedBeamShellMPCElement  # noqa: E402\nfrom anysolver.nonlinear_static import (  # noqa: E402\n    DisplacementControl,\n    _assemble_nonlinear_system,\n)\n\nDC_PARAMS = {\"num_steps\": 12, \"max_iterations\": 40, \"tolerance\": 1.0e-8}\nFC_PARAMS = {\"num_steps\": 6, \"max_iterations\": 30}\n\n\ndef build_model(coupling: str, scale: float):\n    \"\"\"EP isolation geometry; coupling in {'direct','interp'}.\"\"\"\n    m = FEModel(f\"ep_edge_{coupling}\")\n    material(m, scale)\n    grid, nid = {}, 1\n    for ix, x in enumerate(np.linspace(0.0, L, NX + 1)):\n        for iy, y in enumerate(np.linspace(-W / 2, W / 2, NY + 1)):\n            m.add_node(nid, float(x), float(y), 0.0)\n            grid[(ix, iy)] = nid\n            nid += 1\n    eid = 1\n    for ix in range(NX):\n        for iy in range(NY):\n            m.add_element(eid, create_shell_element(\n                eid, [grid[(ix, iy)], grid[(ix + 1, iy)], grid[(ix + 1, iy + 1)], grid[(ix, iy + 1)]],\n                \"steel\", thickness=t))\n            eid += 1\n    n_beam = 2 if coupling == \"direct\" else 3\n    beam_nodes = []\n    for ib, xb in enumerate(np.linspace(0.0, L, n_beam + 1)):\n        b = 100 + ib\n        m.add_node(b, float(xb), -W / 2.0, float(R[2]))\n        beam_nodes.append(b)\n        sx = xb / (L / NX)\n        ix = min(int(np.floor(sx)), NX - 1)\n        xi = sx - ix\n        masters = [(grid[(ix, 0)], 1.0 - xi), (grid[(ix + 1, 0)], xi)]\n        masters = [(n, w) for n, w in masters if w > 1e-12]\n        mid = 200 + ib\n        if len(masters) == 1:\n            m.add_element(mid, CoupledBeamShellElement(mid, b, masters[0][0], \"steel\", eccentricity=R))\n        else:\n            weights = np.array([w for _, w in masters])\n            m.add_element(mid, InterpolatedBeamShellMPCElement(\n                mid, b, [n for n, _ in masters], weights, eccentricity=R))\n    for ib in range(n_beam):\n        m.add_element(300 + ib, BeamElement(300 + ib, [beam_nodes[ib], beam_nodes[ib + 1]], \"steel\", dict(CS)))\n    m.add_boundary_condition(BoundaryCondition(\n        \"root\", [grid[(0, iy)] for iy in range(NY + 1)],\n        {k: 0.0 for k in (\"ux\", \"uy\", \"uz\", \"rx\", \"ry\", \"rz\")}))\n    m.apply_boundary_conditions()\n    lc = LoadCase(\"tip\")\n    probe = grid[(NX, 0)]\n    return m, lc, probe\n\n\ndef add_tip_load(m, lc, fz_per_node):\n    for iy in range(NY + 1):\n        lc.add_nodal_load(grid_node(m, NX, iy), [0, 0, fz_per_node, 0, 0, 0])\n    m.add_load_case(lc)\n\n\ndef grid_node(m, ix, iy):\n    # nodes were added in the same order as build_model; recover by coordinates\n    for node in m.mesh.nodes.values():\n        if (abs(node.x - ix * L / NX) < 1e-12 and abs(node.y + W / 2 - iy * W / NY) < 1e-12\n                and abs(node.z) < 1e-12):\n            return node.id\n    raise KeyError((ix, iy))\n\n\ndef alpha_max(states):\n    vals = [float(np.max(np.abs(s.get(\"alpha\", 0.0)))) for s in states.values() if isinstance(s, dict)]\n    return max(vals, default=0.0)\n\n\ndef independent_residual(model, load_case, u, states, kinematics=\"corotational\"):\n    K0, _ = assemble_stiffness_matrix(model)\n    F_prop, _ = assemble_load_vector(model, load_case)\n    _, _, T, u0, _, _ = build_constraint_transformation(K0, F_prop, model)\n    mpc_map = build_nonlinear_rotating_mpc_map(model, T) if kinematics == \"corotational\" else None\n    states_copy = copy.deepcopy(states)\n    F_int, _, _ = _assemble_nonlinear_system(\n        model, u, states_copy, 5, tangent=False, kinematics=kinematics,\n        corotational_tangent=\"work_conjugate\" if kinematics == \"corotational\" else \"auto\",\n    )\n    lam_force = lambda lam: (mpc_map.reduce_force(u, lam * F_prop - F_int) if mpc_map is not None\n                             else np.asarray(T.T @ (lam * F_prop - F_int)).reshape(-1))\n    ref = (mpc_map.reduce_force(u, F_prop) if mpc_map is not None\n           else np.asarray(T.T @ F_prop).reshape(-1))\n    ref_norm = max(float(np.linalg.norm(ref)), 1.0)\n    return ref_norm, float(np.linalg.norm(lam_force(1.0)))\n\n\ndef uz_of(model, u, probe):\n    return float(u[model.mesh.dof_manager.get_node_dofs(probe)[2]])\n\n\ndef stage_preyield():\n    out = {\"stage\": \"preyield\", \"cases\": []}\n    for coupling in (\"direct\", \"interp\"):\n        row = {\"coupling\": coupling}\n        for label, scale in ((\"plastic\", 1.0), (\"elastic\", 1.0e4)):\n            m, lc, probe = build_model(coupling, scale)\n            add_tip_load(m, lc, -2000.0)\n            res = solve_static_nonlinear(m, lc, kinematics=\"corotational\", **FC_PARAMS)\n            row[label] = {\n                \"status\": res.status,\n                \"load_factor\": res.load_factor,\n                \"uz_probe\": uz_of(m, res.displacements, probe),\n                \"alpha_max\": alpha_max(res.element_states),\n                \"max_eq_plastic_strain\": [s.max_equivalent_plastic_strain for s in res.steps],\n            }\n        row[\"uz_abs_difference\"] = abs(row[\"plastic\"][\"uz_probe\"] - row[\"elastic\"][\"uz_probe\"])\n        out[\"cases\"].append(row)\n        print(json.dumps(row), flush=True)\n    print(json.dumps(out), flush=True)\n\n\ndef dc_solve(coupling, target, num_steps, **extra):\n    m, lc, probe = build_model(coupling, 1.0)\n    add_tip_load(m, lc, -2000.0)\n    control = DisplacementControl(node_id=probe, dof=\"uz\", target_displacement=target)\n    res = solve_static_nonlinear(\n        m, lc, control=\"displacement\", displacement_control=control,\n        kinematics=\"corotational\", num_steps=num_steps,\n        max_iterations=DC_PARAMS[\"max_iterations\"], tolerance=DC_PARAMS[\"tolerance\"],\n        emit_restart_checkpoint=True, record_increment_snapshots=True, **extra,\n    )\n    return m, lc, probe, res\n\n\ndef dc_summary(m, lc, probe, res):\n    uz = uz_of(m, res.displacements, probe)\n    ref_norm, resid = independent_residual(m, lc, res.displacements, res.element_states)\n    reactions = res.steps[-1].support_reactions if res.steps else {}\n    return {\n        \"status\": res.status,\n        \"stop_reason\": res.stop_reason,\n        \"load_factor\": res.load_factor,\n        \"uz_probe\": uz,\n        \"target_error_m\": abs(uz - (-0.20)),\n        \"alpha_max\": alpha_max(res.element_states),\n        \"steps\": [s.to_dict() for s in res.steps],\n        \"snapshot_count\": len(res.snapshots),\n        \"snapshot_control_values\": [s.control_value for s in res.snapshots],\n        \"snapshots_match_steps\": (\n            [s.control_value for s in res.snapshots] == [s.control_value for s in res.steps]\n            and len(res.snapshots) == len(res.steps)\n        ),\n        \"independent_residual_relative\": resid / ref_norm,\n        \"constraint_postcheck\": res.info.get(\"constraint_postcheck\", {}),\n        \"support_reactions\": {k: list(v) for k, v in reactions.items()},\n        \"has_restart_checkpoint\": res.restart_checkpoint is not None,\n    }\n\n\ndef stage_dc_full(coupling):\n    m, lc, probe, res = dc_solve(coupling, -0.20, 12)\n    summary = {\"stage\": \"dc_full\", \"coupling\": coupling, **dc_summary(m, lc, probe, res)}\n    print(json.dumps(summary), flush=True)\n\n\ndef stage_dc_split(coupling):\n    m1, lc1, p1, res1 = dc_solve(coupling, -0.10, 6)\n    half = {\n        \"status\": res1.status, \"load_factor\": res1.load_factor,\n        \"uz_probe\": uz_of(m1, res1.displacements, p1),\n        \"restart_checkpoint_bytes\": len(res1.restart_checkpoint_bytes()),\n    }\n    print(json.dumps({\"stage\": \"dc_split_half\", \"coupling\": coupling, **half}), flush=True)\n\n    m2, lc2, p2, res2 = dc_solve(coupling, -0.20, 6, restart_checkpoint=res1.restart_checkpoint_bytes())\n    m3, lc3, p3, res3 = dc_solve(coupling, -0.20, 12)\n    compare = {\n        \"stage\": \"dc_split_compare\", \"coupling\": coupling,\n        \"resumed\": {\"status\": res2.status, \"load_factor\": res2.load_factor,\n                    \"uz_probe\": uz_of(m2, res2.displacements, p2)},\n        \"uninterrupted\": {\"status\": res3.status, \"load_factor\": res3.load_factor,\n                          \"uz_probe\": uz_of(m3, res3.displacements, p3)},\n        \"displacements_max_abs_diff\": float(np.max(np.abs(res2.displacements - res3.displacements))),\n        \"displacements_exact\": bool(np.array_equal(res2.displacements, res3.displacements)),\n        \"steps_equal\": [s.to_dict() for s in res2.steps] == [s.to_dict() for s in res3.steps],\n        \"load_factor_history_resumed\": [s.load_factor for s in res2.steps],\n        \"load_factor_history_uninterrupted\": [s.load_factor for s in res3.steps],\n        \"restart_bytes_equal\": res2.restart_checkpoint_bytes() == res3.restart_checkpoint_bytes(),\n    }\n    print(json.dumps(compare), flush=True)\n\n\ndef stage_dc_cancel(coupling):\n    m1, lc1, p1, res1 = dc_solve(coupling, -0.10, 6)\n    ckpt_bytes = res1.restart_checkpoint_bytes()\n    ckpt_input = json.loads(ckpt_bytes.decode(\"utf-8\"))\n    ckpt_snapshot = copy.deepcopy(ckpt_input)\n\n    token = CancellationToken()\n    state = {\"steps\": 0}\n\n    def cancel_after_two(status):\n        state[\"steps\"] += 1\n        if state[\"steps\"] >= 2:\n            token.cancel(\"diagnostic cancellation after two status callbacks\")\n\n    cancelled = False\n    try:\n        dc_solve(coupling, -0.20, 6, restart_checkpoint=ckpt_input,\n                 cancellation_token=token, status_callback=cancel_after_two)\n    except Exception as exc:  # noqa: BLE001\n        cancelled = type(exc).__name__ == \"SolveCancelled\"\n        if not cancelled:\n            raise\n    report = {\n        \"stage\": \"dc_cancel\", \"coupling\": coupling,\n        \"cancelled_raised\": cancelled,\n        \"caller_restart_input_unchanged\": _deep_equal_json(ckpt_input, ckpt_snapshot),\n    }\n    # The same checkpoint must still resume cleanly after the cancelled run.\n    m2, lc2, p2, res2 = dc_solve(coupling, -0.20, 6, restart_checkpoint=ckpt_bytes)\n    report[\"checkpoint_still_resumes\"] = res2.status\n    report[\"resumed_load_factor\"] = res2.load_factor\n    report[\"caller_restart_input_still_unchanged\"] = _deep_equal_json(ckpt_input, ckpt_snapshot)\n    print(json.dumps(report), flush=True)\n\n\ndef _deep_equal_json(a, b):\n    return json.dumps(a, sort_keys=True) == json.dumps(b, sort_keys=True)\n\n\ndef main():\n    stage = sys.argv[1]\n    if stage == \"preyield\":\n        stage_preyield()\n    elif stage == \"dc_full\":\n        stage_dc_full(sys.argv[2])\n    elif stage == \"dc_split\":\n        stage_dc_split(sys.argv[2])\n    elif stage == \"dc_cancel\":\n        stage_dc_cancel(sys.argv[2])\n    else:\n        raise SystemExit(f\"unknown stage {stage!r}\")\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n", "suffix": "", "verb": "Creating", "message": "C:\\Github\\ANYsolver\\.development\\nonlinear-master-slave-coupling-20261017\\diagnostics\\ep_edge_coupling.py", "settledVerb": "Created", "settledMessage": "C:\\Github\\ANYsolver\\.development\\nonlinear-master-slave-coupling-20261017\\diagnostics\\ep_edge_coupling.py", "statusText": "Writing file"}, "kind": "file_write", "input": {"filePath": "C:\\Github\\ANYsolver\\.development\\nonlinear-master-slave-coupling-20261017\\diagnostics\\ep_edge_coupling.py", "content": "\"\"\"Slice 3 deliverable 3: direct vs interpolated edge coupling, EP geometry.\n\nExisting EP isolation geometry and repository S355 curve (ep_isolation.py):\nL=1.0, W=0.24, t=0.012, shell 2x1, stiffener 10x40 mm at e=+0.04,\nfiber plasticity. Direct coupling: beam with 2 elements (nodes on shell\nedge nodes). Interpolated counterpart: beam with 3 elements (middle nodes\ngenuinely interpolated on the edge).\n\nStages (streamed as JSON, one per line, flush immediately):\n  preyield                 -2 kN/node force control, plastic vs elastic,\n                            direct and interpolated: lambda=1, zero plastic\n                            strain, plastic == elastic control.\n  dc_full DIRECT|INTERP    uninterrupted DC uz=-0.20 at the original tip\n                            probe (num_steps=12, max_iterations=40,\n                            tolerance=1e-8): completion, target error,\n                            positive plastic strain, independent reduced\n                            residual, constraint postcheck, reactions.\n  dc_split DIRECT|INTERP  split at uz=-0.10, resume to -0.20, compare\n                            u/lambda/history with the uninterrupted run\n                            (same tolerances, no relaxation).\n  dc_cancel DIRECT         cancellation during a resumed run: caller restart\n                            input deep-unchanged, accepted snapshots only\n                            from committed steps, checkpoint still resumes.\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport copy\nimport json\nimport os\nimport sys\n\nsys.path.insert(0, os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__)))\n\nimport numpy as np\n\nfrom ep_isolation import CS, L, NX, NY, R, W, material, t  # noqa: E402\nfrom anysolver import (  # noqa: E402\n    BoundaryCondition,\n    FEModel,\n    LoadCase,\n    create_shell_element,\n    solve_static_nonlinear,\n)\nfrom anysolver.assembly import build_constraint_transformation  # noqa: E402\nfrom anysolver.control import CancellationToken  # noqa: E402\nfrom anysolver.corotational import build_nonlinear_rotating_mpc_map  # noqa: E402\nfrom anysolver.elements import BeamElement, CoupledBeamShellElement  # noqa: E402\nfrom anysolver.matrix_assembly import (  # noqa: E402\n    assemble_load_vector,\n    assemble_stiffness_matrix,\n)\nfrom anysolver.mesh_gen import InterpolatedBeamShellMPCElement  # noqa: E402\nfrom anysolver.nonlinear_static import (  # noqa: E402\n    DisplacementControl,\n    _assemble_nonlinear_system,\n)\n\nDC_PARAMS = {\"num_steps\": 12, \"max_iterations\": 40, \"tolerance\": 1.0e-8}\nFC_PARAMS = {\"num_steps\": 6, \"max_iterations\": 30}\n\n\ndef build_model(coupling: str, scale: float):\n    \"\"\"EP isolation geometry; coupling in {'direct','interp'}.\"\"\"\n    m = FEModel(f\"ep_edge_{coupling}\")\n    material(m, scale)\n    grid, nid = {}, 1\n    for ix, x in enumerate(np.linspace(0.0, L, NX + 1)):\n        for iy, y in enumerate(np.linspace(-W / 2, W / 2, NY + 1)):\n            m.add_node(nid, float(x), float(y), 0.0)\n            grid[(ix, iy)] = nid\n            nid += 1\n    eid = 1\n    for ix in range(NX):\n        for iy in range(NY):\n            m.add_element(eid, create_shell_element(\n                eid, [grid[(ix, iy)], grid[(ix + 1, iy)], grid[(ix + 1, iy + 1)], grid[(ix, iy + 1)]],\n                \"steel\", thickness=t))\n            eid += 1\n    n_beam = 2 if coupling == \"direct\" else 3\n    beam_nodes = []\n    for ib, xb in enumerate(np.linspace(0.0, L, n_beam + 1)):\n        b = 100 + ib\n        m.add_node(b, float(xb), -W / 2.0, float(R[2]))\n        beam_nodes.append(b)\n        sx = xb / (L / NX)\n        ix = min(int(np.floor(sx)), NX - 1)\n        xi = sx - ix\n        masters = [(grid[(ix, 0)], 1.0 - xi), (grid[(ix + 1, 0)], xi)]\n        masters = [(n, w) for n, w in masters if w > 1e-12]\n        mid = 200 + ib\n        if len(masters) == 1:\n            m.add_element(mid, CoupledBeamShellElement(mid, b, masters[0][0], \"steel\", eccentricity=R))\n        else:\n            weights = np.array([w for _, w in masters])\n            m.add_element(mid, InterpolatedBeamShellMPCElement(\n                mid, b, [n for n, _ in masters], weights, eccentricity=R))\n    for ib in range(n_beam):\n        m.add_element(300 + ib, BeamElement(300 + ib, [beam_nodes[ib], beam_nodes[ib + 1]], \"steel\", dict(CS)))\n    m.add_boundary_condition(BoundaryCondition(\n        \"root\", [grid[(0, iy)] for iy in range(NY + 1)],\n        {k: 0.0 for k in (\"ux\", \"uy\", \"uz\", \"rx\", \"ry\", \"rz\")}))\n    m.apply_boundary_conditions()\n    lc = LoadCase(\"tip\")\n    probe = grid[(NX, 0)]\n    return m, lc, probe\n\n\ndef add_tip_load(m, lc, fz_per_node):\n    for iy in range(NY + 1):\n        lc.add_nodal_load(grid_node(m, NX, iy), [0, 0, fz_per_node, 0, 0, 0])\n    m.add_load_case(lc)\n\n\ndef grid_node(m, ix, iy):\n    # nodes were added in the same order as build_model; recover by coordinates\n    for node in m.mesh.nodes.values():\n        if (abs(node.x - ix * L / NX) < 1e-12 and abs(node.y + W / 2 - iy * W / NY) < 1e-12\n                and abs(node.z) < 1e-12):\n            return node.id\n    raise KeyError((ix, iy))\n\n\ndef alpha_max(states):\n    vals = [float(np.max(np.abs(s.get(\"alpha\", 0.0)))) for s in states.values() if isinstance(s, dict)]\n    return max(vals, default=0.0)\n\n\ndef independent_residual(model, load_case, u, states, kinematics=\"corotational\"):\n    K0, _ = assemble_stiffness_matrix(model)\n    F_prop, _ = assemble_load_vector(model, load_case)\n    _, _, T, u0, _, _ = build_constraint_transformation(K0, F_prop, model)\n    mpc_map = build_nonlinear_rotating_mpc_map(model, T) if kinematics == \"corotational\" else None\n    states_copy = copy.deepcopy(states)\n    F_int, _, _ = _assemble_nonlinear_system(\n        model, u, states_copy, 5, tangent=False, kinematics=kinematics,\n        corotational_tangent=\"work_conjugate\" if kinematics == \"corotational\" else \"auto\",\n    )\n    lam_force = lambda lam: (mpc_map.reduce_force(u, lam * F_prop - F_int) if mpc_map is not None\n                             else np.asarray(T.T @ (lam * F_prop - F_int)).reshape(-1))\n    ref = (mpc_map.reduce_force(u, F_prop) if mpc_map is not None\n           else np.asarray(T.T @ F_prop).reshape(-1))\n    ref_norm = max(float(np.linalg.norm(ref)), 1.0)\n    return ref_norm, float(np.linalg.norm(lam_force(1.0)))\n\n\ndef uz_of(model, u, probe):\n    return float(u[model.mesh.dof_manager.get_node_dofs(probe)[2]])\n\n\ndef stage_preyield():\n    out = {\"stage\": \"preyield\", \"cases\": []}\n    for coupling in (\"direct\", \"interp\"):\n        row = {\"coupling\": coupling}\n        for label, scale in ((\"plastic\", 1.0), (\"elastic\", 1.0e4)):\n            m, lc, probe = build_model(coupling, scale)\n            add_tip_load(m, lc, -2000.0)\n            res = solve_static_nonlinear(m, lc, kinematics=\"corotational\", **FC_PARAMS)\n            row[label] = {\n                \"status\": res.status,\n                \"load_factor\": res.load_factor,\n                \"uz_probe\": uz_of(m, res.displacements, probe),\n                \"alpha_max\": alpha_max(res.element_states),\n                \"max_eq_plastic_strain\": [s.max_equivalent_plastic_strain for s in res.steps],\n            }\n        row[\"uz_abs_difference\"] = abs(row[\"plastic\"][\"uz_probe\"] - row[\"elastic\"][\"uz_probe\"])\n        out[\"cases\"].append(row)\n        print(json.dumps(row), flush=True)\n    print(json.dumps(out), flush=True)\n\n\ndef dc_solve(coupling, target, num_steps, **extra):\n    m, lc, probe = build_model(coupling, 1.0)\n    add_tip_load(m, lc, -2000.0)\n    control = DisplacementControl(node_id=probe, dof=\"uz\", target_displacement=target)\n    res = solve_static_nonlinear(\n        m, lc, control=\"displacement\", displacement_control=control,\n        kinematics=\"corotational\", num_steps=num_steps,\n        max_iterations=DC_PARAMS[\"max_iterations\"], tolerance=DC_PARAMS[\"tolerance\"],\n        emit_restart_checkpoint=True, record_increment_snapshots=True, **extra,\n    )\n    return m, lc, probe, res\n\n\ndef dc_summary(m, lc, probe, res):\n    uz = uz_of(m, res.displacements, probe)\n    ref_norm, resid = independent_residual(m, lc, res.displacements, res.element_states)\n    reactions = res.steps[-1].support_reactions if res.steps else {}\n    return {\n        \"status\": res.status,\n        \"stop_reason\": res.stop_reason,\n        \"load_factor\": res.load_factor,\n        \"uz_probe\": uz,\n        \"target_error_m\": abs(uz - (-0.20)),\n        \"alpha_max\": alpha_max(res.element_states),\n        \"steps\": [s.to_dict() for s in res.steps],\n        \"snapshot_count\": len(res.snapshots),\n        \"snapshot_control_values\": [s.control_value for s in res.snapshots],\n        \"snapshots_match_steps\": (\n            [s.control_value for s in res.snapshots] == [s.control_value for s in res.steps]\n            and len(res.snapshots) == len(res.steps)\n        ),\n        \"independent_residual_relative\": resid / ref_norm,\n        \"constraint_postcheck\": res.info.get(\"constraint_postcheck\", {}),\n        \"support_reactions\": {k: list(v) for k, v in reactions.items()},\n        \"has_restart_checkpoint\": res.restart_checkpoint is not None,\n    }\n\n\ndef stage_dc_full(coupling):\n    m, lc, probe, res = dc_solve(coupling, -0.20, 12)\n    summary = {\"stage\": \"dc_full\", \"coupling\": coupling, **dc_summary(m, lc, probe, res)}\n    print(json.dumps(summary), flush=True)\n\n\ndef stage_dc_split(coupling):\n    m1, lc1, p1, res1 = dc_solve(coupling, -0.10, 6)\n    half = {\n        \"status\": res1.status, \"load_factor\": res1.load_factor,\n        \"uz_probe\": uz_of(m1, res1.displacements, p1),\n        \"restart_checkpoint_bytes\": len(res1.restart_checkpoint_bytes()),\n    }\n    print(json.dumps({\"stage\": \"dc_split_half\", \"coupling\": coupling, **half}), flush=True)\n\n    m2, lc2, p2, res2 = dc_solve(coupling, -0.20, 6, restart_checkpoint=res1.restart_checkpoint_bytes())\n    m3, lc3, p3, res3 = dc_solve(coupling, -0.20, 12)\n    compare = {\n        \"stage\": \"dc_split_compare\", \"coupling\": coupling,\n        \"resumed\": {\"status\": res2.status, \"load_factor\": res2.load_factor,\n                    \"uz_probe\": uz_of(m2, res2.displacements, p2)},\n        \"uninterrupted\": {\"status\": res3.status, \"load_factor\": res3.load_factor,\n                          \"uz_probe\": uz_of(m3, res3.displacements, p3)},\n        \"displacements_max_abs_diff\": float(np.max(np.abs(res2.displacements - res3.displacements))),\n        \"displacements_exact\": bool(np.array_equal(res2.displacements, res3.displacements)),\n        \"steps_equal\": [s.to_dict() for s in res2.steps] == [s.to_dict() for s in res3.steps],\n        \"load_factor_history_resumed\": [s.load_factor for s in res2.steps],\n        \"load_factor_history_uninterrupted\": [s.load_factor for s in res3.steps],\n        \"restart_bytes_equal\": res2.restart_checkpoint_bytes() == res3.restart_checkpoint_bytes(),\n    }\n    print(json.dumps(compare), flush=True)\n\n\ndef stage_dc_cancel(coupling):\n    m1, lc1, p1, res1 = dc_solve(coupling, -0.10, 6)\n    ckpt_bytes = res1.restart_checkpoint_bytes()\n    ckpt_input = json.loads(ckpt_bytes.decode(\"utf-8\"))\n    ckpt_snapshot = copy.deepcopy(ckpt_input)\n\n    token = CancellationToken()\n    state = {\"steps\": 0}\n\n    def cancel_after_two(status):\n        state[\"steps\"] += 1\n        if state[\"steps\"] >= 2:\n            token.cancel(\"diagnostic cancellation after two status callbacks\")\n\n    cancelled = False\n    try:\n        dc_solve(coupling, -0.20, 6, restart_checkpoint=ckpt_input,\n                 cancellation_token=token, status_callback=cancel_after_two)\n    except Exception as exc:  # noqa: BLE001\n        cancelled = type(exc).__name__ == \"SolveCancelled\"\n        if not cancelled:\n            raise\n    report = {\n        \"stage\": \"dc_cancel\", \"coupling\": coupling,\n        \"cancelled_raised\": cancelled,\n        \"caller_restart_input_unchanged\": _deep_equal_json(ckpt_input, ckpt_snapshot),\n    }\n    # The same checkpoint must still resume cleanly after the cancelled run.\n    m2, lc2, p2, res2 = dc_solve(coupling, -0.20, 6, restart_checkpoint=ckpt_bytes)\n    report[\"checkpoint_still_resumes\"] = res2.status\n    report[\"resumed_load_factor\"] = res2.load_factor\n    report[\"caller_restart_input_still_unchanged\"] = _deep_equal_json(ckpt_input, ckpt_snapshot)\n    print(json.dumps(report), flush=True)\n\n\ndef _deep_equal_json(a, b):\n    return json.dumps(a, sort_keys=True) == json.dumps(b, sort_keys=True)\n\n\ndef main():\n    stage = sys.argv[1]\n    if stage == \"preyield\":\n        stage_preyield()\n    elif stage == \"dc_full\":\n        stage_dc_full(sys.argv[2])\n    elif stage == \"dc_split\":\n        stage_dc_split(sys.argv[2])\n    elif stage == \"dc_cancel\":\n        stage_dc_cancel(sys.argv[2])\n    else:\n        raise SystemExit(f\"unknown stage {stage!r}\")\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n"}}, "state": {"status": "completed", "output": {"filePath": "C:\\Github\\ANYsolver\\.development\\nonlinear-master-slave-coupling-20261017\\diagnostics\\ep_edge_coupling.py", "content": "\"\"\"Slice 3 deliverable 3: direct vs interpolated edge coupling, EP geometry.\n\nExisting EP isolation geometry and repository S355 curve (ep_isolation.py):\nL=1.0, W=0.24, t=0.012, shell 2x1, stiffener 10x40 mm at e=+0.04,\nfiber plasticity. Direct coupling: beam with 2 elements (nodes on shell\nedge nodes). Interpolated counterpart: beam with 3 elements (middle nodes\ngenuinely interpolated on the edge).\n\nStages (streamed as JSON, one per line, flush immediately):\n  preyield                 -2 kN/node force control, plastic vs elastic,\n                            direct and interpolated: lambda=1, zero plastic\n                            strain, plastic == elastic control.\n  dc_full DIRECT|INTERP    uninterrupted DC uz=-0.20 at the original tip\n                            probe (num_steps=12, max_iterations=40,\n                            tolerance=1e-8): completion, target error,\n                            positive plastic strain, independent reduced\n                            residual, constraint postcheck, reactions.\n  dc_split DIRECT|INTERP  split at uz=-0.10, resume to -0.20, compare\n                            u/lambda/history with the uninterrupted run\n                            (same tolerances, no relaxation).\n  dc_cancel DIRECT         cancellation during a resumed run: caller restart\n                            input deep-unchanged, accepted snapshots only\n                            from committed steps, checkpoint still resumes.\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport copy\nimport json\nimport os\nimport sys\n\nsys.path.insert(0, os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__)))\n\nimport numpy as np\n\nfrom ep_isolation import CS, L, NX, NY, R, W, material, t  # noqa: E402\nfrom anysolver import (  # noqa: E402\n    BoundaryCondition,\n    FEModel,\n    LoadCase,\n    create_shell_element,\n    solve_static_nonlinear,\n)\nfrom anysolver.assembly import build_constraint_transformation  # noqa: E402\nfrom anysolver.control import CancellationToken  # noqa: E402\nfrom anysolver.corotational import build_nonlinear_rotating_mpc_map  # noqa: E402\nfrom anysolver.elements import BeamElement, CoupledBeamShellElement  # noqa: E402\nfrom anysolver.matrix_assembly import (  # noqa: E402\n    assemble_load_vector,\n    assemble_stiffness_matrix,\n)\nfrom anysolver.mesh_gen import InterpolatedBeamShellMPCElement  # noqa: E402\nfrom anysolver.nonlinear_static import (  # noqa: E402\n    DisplacementControl,\n    _assemble_nonlinear_system,\n)\n\nDC_PARAMS = {\"num_steps\": 12, \"max_iterations\": 40, \"tolerance\": 1.0e-8}\nFC_PARAMS = {\"num_steps\": 6, \"max_iterations\": 30}\n\n\ndef build_model(coupling: str, scale: float):\n    \"\"\"EP isolation geometry; coupling in {'direct','interp'}.\"\"\"\n    m = FEModel(f\"ep_edge_{coupling}\")\n    material(m, scale)\n    grid, nid = {}, 1\n    for ix, x in enumerate(np.linspace(0.0, L, NX + 1)):\n        for iy, y in enumerate(np.linspace(-W / 2, W / 2, NY + 1)):\n            m.add_node(nid, float(x), float(y), 0.0)\n            grid[(ix, iy)] = nid\n            nid += 1\n    eid = 1\n    for ix in range(NX):\n        for iy in range(NY):\n            m.add_element(eid, create_shell_element(\n                eid, [grid[(ix, iy)], grid[(ix + 1, iy)], grid[(ix + 1, iy + 1)], grid[(ix, iy + 1)]],\n                \"steel\", thickness=t))\n            eid += 1\n    n_beam = 2 if coupling == \"direct\" else 3\n    beam_nodes = []\n    for ib, xb in enumerate(np.linspace(0.0, L, n_beam + 1)):\n        b = 100 + ib\n        m.add_node(b, float(xb), -W / 2.0, float(R[2]))\n        beam_nodes.append(b)\n        sx = xb / (L / NX)\n        ix = min(int(np.floor(sx)), NX - 1)\n        xi = sx - ix\n        masters = [(grid[(ix, 0)], 1.0 - xi), (grid[(ix + 1, 0)], xi)]\n        masters = [(n, w) for n, w in masters if w > 1e-12]\n        mid = 200 + ib\n        if len(masters) == 1:\n            m.add_element(mid, CoupledBeamShellElement(mid, b, masters[0][0], \"steel\", eccentricity=R))\n        else:\n            weights = np.array([w for _, w in masters])\n            m.add_element(mid, InterpolatedBeamShellMPCElement(\n                mid, b, [n for n, _ in masters], weights, eccentricity=R))\n    for ib in range(n_beam):\n        m.add_element(300 + ib, BeamElement(300 + ib, [beam_nodes[ib], beam_nodes[ib + 1]], \"steel\", dict(CS)))\n    m.add_boundary_condition(BoundaryCondition(\n        \"root\", [grid[(0, iy)] for iy in range(NY + 1)],\n        {k: 0.0 for k in (\"ux\", \"uy\", \"uz\", \"rx\", \"ry\", \"rz\")}))\n    m.apply_boundary_conditions()\n    lc = LoadCase(\"tip\")\n    probe = grid[(NX, 0)]\n    return m, lc, probe\n\n\ndef add_tip_load(m, lc, fz_per_node):\n    for iy in range(NY + 1):\n        lc.add_nodal_load(grid_node(m, NX, iy), [0, 0, fz_per_node, 0, 0, 0])\n    m.add_load_case(lc)\n\n\ndef grid_node(m, ix, iy):\n    # nodes were added in the same order as build_model; recover by coordinates\n    for node in m.mesh.nodes.values():\n        if (abs(node.x - ix * L / NX) < 1e-12 and abs(node.y + W / 2 - iy * W / NY) < 1e-12\n                and abs(node.z) < 1e-12):\n            return node.id\n    raise KeyError((ix, iy))\n\n\ndef alpha_max(states):\n    vals = [float(np.max(np.abs(s.get(\"alpha\", 0.0)))) for s in states.values() if isinstance(s, dict)]\n    return max(vals, default=0.0)\n\n\ndef independent_residual(model, load_case, u, states, kinematics=\"corotational\"):\n    K0, _ = assemble_stiffness_matrix(model)\n    F_prop, _ = assemble_load_vector(model, load_case)\n    _, _, T, u0, _, _ = build_constraint_transformation(K0, F_prop, model)\n    mpc_map = build_nonlinear_rotating_mpc_map(model, T) if kinematics == \"corotational\" else None\n    states_copy = copy.deepcopy(states)\n    F_int, _, _ = _assemble_nonlinear_system(\n        model, u, states_copy, 5, tangent=False, kinematics=kinematics,\n        corotational_tangent=\"work_conjugate\" if kinematics == \"corotational\" else \"auto\",\n    )\n    lam_force = lambda lam: (mpc_map.reduce_force(u, lam * F_prop - F_int) if mpc_map is not None\n                             else np.asarray(T.T @ (lam * F_prop - F_int)).reshape(-1))\n    ref = (mpc_map.reduce_force(u, F_prop) if mpc_map is not None\n           else np.asarray(T.T @ F_prop).reshape(-1))\n    ref_norm = max(float(np.linalg.norm(ref)), 1.0)\n    return ref_norm, float(np.linalg.norm(lam_force(1.0)))\n\n\ndef uz_of(model, u, probe):\n    return float(u[model.mesh.dof_manager.get_node_dofs(probe)[2]])\n\n\ndef stage_preyield():\n    out = {\"stage\": \"preyield\", \"cases\": []}\n    for coupling in (\"direct\", \"interp\"):\n        row = {\"coupling\": coupling}\n        for label, scale in ((\"plastic\", 1.0), (\"elastic\", 1.0e4)):\n            m, lc, probe = build_model(coupling, scale)\n            add_tip_load(m, lc, -2000.0)\n            res = solve_static_nonlinear(m, lc, kinematics=\"corotational\", **FC_PARAMS)\n            row[label] = {\n                \"status\": res.status,\n                \"load_factor\": res.load_factor,\n                \"uz_probe\": uz_of(m, res.displacements, probe),\n                \"alpha_max\": alpha_max(res.element_states),\n                \"max_eq_plastic_strain\": [s.max_equivalent_plastic_strain for s in res.steps],\n            }\n        row[\"uz_abs_difference\"] = abs(row[\"plastic\"][\"uz_probe\"] - row[\"elastic\"][\"uz_probe\"])\n        out[\"cases\"].append(row)\n        print(json.dumps(row), flush=True)\n    print(json.dumps(out), flush=True)\n\n\ndef dc_solve(coupling, target, num_steps, **extra):\n    m, lc, probe = build_model(coupling, 1.0)\n    add_tip_load(m, lc, -2000.0)\n    control = DisplacementControl(node_id=probe, dof=\"uz\", target_displacement=target)\n    res = solve_static_nonlinear(\n        m, lc, control=\"displacement\", displacement_control=control,\n        kinematics=\"corotational\", num_steps=num_steps,\n        max_iterations=DC_PARAMS[\"max_iterations\"], tolerance=DC_PARAMS[\"tolerance\"],\n        emit_restart_checkpoint=True, record_increment_snapshots=True, **extra,\n    )\n    return m, lc, probe, res\n\n\ndef dc_summary(m, lc, probe, res):\n    uz = uz_of(m, res.displacements, probe)\n    ref_norm, resid = independent_residual(m, lc, res.displacements, res.element_states)\n    reactions = res.steps[-1].support_reactions if res.steps else {}\n    return {\n        \"status\": res.status,\n        \"stop_reason\": res.stop_reason,\n        \"load_factor\": res.load_factor,\n        \"uz_probe\": uz,\n        \"target_error_m\": abs(uz - (-0.20)),\n        \"alpha_max\": alpha_max(res.element_states),\n        \"steps\": [s.to_dict() for s in res.steps],\n        \"snapshot_count\": len(res.snapshots),\n        \"snapshot_control_values\": [s.control_value for s in res.snapshots],\n        \"snapshots_match_steps\": (\n            [s.control_value for s in res.snapshots] == [s.control_value for s in res.steps]\n            and len(res.snapshots) == len(res.steps)\n        ),\n        \"independent_residual_relative\": resid / ref_norm,\n        \"constraint_postcheck\": res.info.get(\"constraint_postcheck\", {}),\n        \"support_reactions\": {k: list(v) for k, v in reactions.items()},\n        \"has_restart_checkpoint\": res.restart_checkpoint is not None,\n    }\n\n\ndef stage_dc_full(coupling):\n    m, lc, probe, res = dc_solve(coupling, -0.20, 12)\n    summary = {\"stage\": \"dc_full\", \"coupling\": coupling, **dc_summary(m, lc, probe, res)}\n    print(json.dumps(summary), flush=True)\n\n\ndef stage_dc_split(coupling):\n    m1, lc1, p1, res1 = dc_solve(coupling, -0.10, 6)\n    half = {\n        \"status\": res1.status, \"load_factor\": res1.load_factor,\n        \"uz_probe\": uz_of(m1, res1.displacements, p1),\n        \"restart_checkpoint_bytes\": len(res1.restart_checkpoint_bytes()),\n    }\n    print(json.dumps({\"stage\": \"dc_split_half\", \"coupling\": coupling, **half}), flush=True)\n\n    m2, lc2, p2, res2 = dc_solve(coupling, -0.20, 6, restart_checkpoint=res1.restart_checkpoint_bytes())\n    m3, lc3, p3, res3 = dc_solve(coupling, -0.20, 12)\n    compare = {\n        \"stage\": \"dc_split_compare\", \"coupling\": coupling,\n        \"resumed\": {\"status\": res2.status, \"load_factor\": res2.load_factor,\n                    \"uz_probe\": uz_of(m2, res2.displacements, p2)},\n        \"uninterrupted\": {\"status\": res3.status, \"load_factor\": res3.load_factor,\n                          \"uz_probe\": uz_of(m3, res3.displacements, p3)},\n        \"displacements_max_abs_diff\": float(np.max(np.abs(res2.displacements - res3.displacements))),\n        \"displacements_exact\": bool(np.array_equal(res2.displacements, res3.displacements)),\n        \"steps_equal\": [s.to_dict() for s in res2.steps] == [s.to_dict() for s in res3.steps],\n        \"load_factor_history_resumed\": [s.load_factor for s in res2.steps],\n        \"load_factor_history_uninterrupted\": [s.load_factor for s in res3.steps],\n        \"restart_bytes_equal\": res2.restart_checkpoint_bytes() == res3.restart_checkpoint_bytes(),\n    }\n    print(json.dumps(compare), flush=True)\n\n\ndef stage_dc_cancel(coupling):\n    m1, lc1, p1, res1 = dc_solve(coupling, -0.10, 6)\n    ckpt_bytes = res1.restart_checkpoint_bytes()\n    ckpt_input = json.loads(ckpt_bytes.decode(\"utf-8\"))\n    ckpt_snapshot = copy.deepcopy(ckpt_input)\n\n    token = CancellationToken()\n    state = {\"steps\": 0}\n\n    def cancel_after_two(status):\n        state[\"steps\"] += 1\n        if state[\"steps\"] >= 2:\n            token.cancel(\"diagnostic cancellation after two status callbacks\")\n\n    cancelled = False\n    try:\n        dc_solve(coupling, -0.20, 6, restart_checkpoint=ckpt_input,\n                 cancellation_token=token, status_callback=cancel_after_two)\n    except Exception as exc:  # noqa: BLE001\n        cancelled = type(exc).__name__ == \"SolveCancelled\"\n        if not cancelled:\n            raise\n    report = {\n        \"stage\": \"dc_cancel\", \"coupling\": coupling,\n        \"cancelled_raised\": cancelled,\n        \"caller_restart_input_unchanged\": _deep_equal_json(ckpt_input, ckpt_snapshot),\n    }\n    # The same checkpoint must still resume cleanly after the cancelled run.\n    m2, lc2, p2, res2 = dc_solve(coupling, -0.20, 6, restart_checkpoint=ckpt_bytes)\n    report[\"checkpoint_still_resumes\"] = res2.status\n    report[\"resumed_load_factor\"] = res2.load_factor\n    report[\"caller_restart_input_still_unchanged\"] = _deep_equal_json(ckpt_input, ckpt_snapshot)\n    print(json.dumps(report), flush=True)\n\n\ndef _deep_equal_json(a, b):\n    return json.dumps(a, sort_keys=True) == json.dumps(b, sort_keys=True)\n\n\ndef main():\n    stage = sys.argv[1]\n    if stage == \"preyield\":\n        stage_preyield()\n    elif stage == \"dc_full\":\n        stage_dc_full(sys.argv[2])\n    elif stage == \"dc_split\":\n        stage_dc_split(sys.argv[2])\n    elif stage == \"dc_cancel\":\n        stage_dc_cancel(sys.argv[2])\n    else:\n        raise SystemExit(f\"unknown stage {stage!r}\")\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n"}, "outputText": "", "durationMs": 0.0, "display": {"success": true, "verb": "Created", "message": "C:\\Github\\ANYsolver\\.development\\nonlinear-master-slave-coupling-20261017\\diagnostics\\ep_edge_coupling.py", "warnings": [], "approvalNote": null, "suffix": ""}, "decision": "execute", "approvalType": "always", "approvalSource": "bypass"}}
{"id": "reasoning-e601d7e2-c763-5bdd-aef6-bf55adee2f5f-0", "sessionId": "b9a80757-48a2-a90d-2f72-692761706b93", "turnId": "turn-8c7e0354138e253f073f636b837c66de", "createdAt": 1792346368424, "updatedAt": 1792346368424, "generationStatus": "completed", "relatedEntryId": null, "type": "reasoning", "text": "Wait, there's a bug: `add_tip_load` uses `grid_node(m, NX, iy)` but `grid` local dict isn't accessible outside build_model. I wrote grid_node to recover by coordinates — but the y-coordinate check: `abs(node.y + W/2 - iy*W/NY)` — nodes at y = -W/2 + iy*(W/NY)? np.linspace(-W/2, W/2, NY+1): y_i = -W/2 + i*(W/NY). Yes correct. And x: ix*L/NX. OK.\n\nBut also in build_model I don't add the load case — add_tip_load calls m.add_load_case(lc). Good.\n\nOne issue: `dc_solve` passes `status_callback` in stage_dc_cancel via **extra — solve_static_nonlinear accepts status_callback. Good.\n\nAnother: in stage_dc_cancel, dc_solve with restart_checkpoint=ckpt_input (dict). The API accepts bytes or dict? test uses restart_checkpoint=first.restart_checkpoint_bytes() (bytes) and also raw=... Let me check what types restart_checkpoint accepts — line 198 in the test: `restart_checkpoint=raw` where raw = first.restart_checkpoint_bytes(). And line 242: restart_checkpoint=first.restart_checkpoint_bytes(). The validation may accept dict too (validated_restart.path_state suggests parsing). To be safe, pass the dict — if it rejects, I'll see an error and switch to bytes + verify bytes immutability (trivially immutable). Actually the point is \"caller restart inputs\" unchanged — bytes are trivially immutable, so passing a dict is the stronger test. If dict isn't accepted, fall back.\n\nAlso `InterpolatedBeamShellMPCElement` signature: (mid, b, masters, weights, eccentricity=r) — from convergence_study: `InterpolatedBeamShellMPCElement(mid, b, masters, weights, eccentricity=r)`. Good.\n\nCS from ep_isolation includes \"fiber_plasticity\": True. Good.\n\nOne concern: preyield stage — the elastic control uses scale=1e4 (yield × 1e4). At -2k/node, is the response below yield for scale 1.0? HANDOVER sweep: at -2000, EP == elastic exactly, alpha 0. Good.\n\nAlso `material()` import from ep_isolation — it's defined there taking (model, scale). Good. And `t` is the shell thickness variable name in ep_isolation (t=0.012). I import L, W, t, NX, NY, R, CS, material. ep_isolation has L, W, t = 1.0, 0.24, 0.012 and NX, NY = 2, 1, R, CS. Good.\n\nCompile check then run preyield.", "summary": []}
